cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "VSLAM-Based Navigation for Autonomous Sidewalk Robots"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zin
    given-names: Thaw
    affiliation: "McMaster University (Mitacs Globalink 2026)"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: 2026-09-30
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Thawzin1/vslam-sidewalk-robot"
abstract: >-
  Visual SLAM (RTAB-Map with a ZED X stereo camera, blended with wheel and gyroscope readings) for a
  Clearpath Husky A200 sidewalk robot on a Jetson AGX Orin: mapping, localisation on a saved map,
  continued mapping sessions and goal-driven navigation, evaluated against an independent LiDAR
  estimate. Mitacs Globalink 2026 project at McMaster University, supervised by Prof. Moein Mehrtash.
keywords:
  - visual SLAM
  - RTAB-Map
  - ZED X
  - Husky A200
  - sidewalk robot
  - ROS Noetic
references:
  - type: article
    title: "RTAB-Map as an open-source lidar and visual SLAM library for large-scale and long-term online operation"
    authors:
      - family-names: Labbé
        given-names: Mathieu
      - family-names: Michaud
        given-names: François
    journal: "Journal of Field Robotics"
    volume: 36
    issue: 2
    year: 2019
    doi: 10.1002/rob.21831
